# SEO Standards

Designs HTML has **titles only** (no meta descriptions). Every Next.js route must ship full metadata.

## Per-page metadata (App Router)

```tsx
import type { Metadata } from "next";

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: "Pricing | Suricat",
  description: "…unique 140–160 char summary…",
  openGraph: {
    title: "Pricing | Suricat",
    description: "…",
    type: "website",
  },
  twitter: {
    card: "summary_large_image",
    title: "Pricing | Suricat",
    description: "…",
  },
};
```

Root layout: set `metadataBase`, default `title.template` (`%s | Suricat`), and site-wide defaults. Page titles override uniquely.

## Title conventions

- Pattern: `{Page Name} | Suricat` (home: `Suricat | The Compliance Intelligence Platform`)
- Fix bad Designs titles: `readiness.html` `"Home"` → proper readiness title; align about page vs home

## Heading hierarchy

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Exactly **one** `<h1>` per page | Page hero / primary topic |
| Sections use `<h2>` | Not `h4` first for card titles |
| Subsections `<h3>` | Cards / feature titles under an `h2` |
| Body copy `<p>` | Never fake paragraphs with `div` for SEO text |
| Eyebrows | `<p>` or `<span>`, not headings |

```tsx
// ✅
<section>
  <h2>…</h2>
  <p>…</p>
  <article><h3>…</h3><p>…</p></article>
</section>
```

## Technical SEO

- `<html lang="en">`
- Meaningful `alt` on content images; decorative → `alt=""`
- Use `next/link` for internal links; logical URL structure (see route map in design-system plan)
- Prefer server-rendered text in headings (not image-only titles)
